Correction to the brief: the brief suggested 500x333. Odd dims are refused
by the `raw:` I420 layout on both harnesses (floor chroma; `perf_encode`
asserts even dims, as does `identity_run raw:`), so the non-aligned cell is
500x332 — still non-64-aligned on both axes, which is the property that
mattered. An odd-height real-content cell would need the byte harness's
ceiling-chroma path, which the perf harness does not have.

=================== BYTE-IDENTITY PER CELL ===================

Two checks per cell, as in the prior records: (1) an uninstrumented pre-pass
(port writes .yuv+.obu, C reads the same .yuv, `cmp`); (2) each callgrind
run's OWN .obu `cmp`'d against the pre-pass. (2) passed on all 36 runs.

