    64 = 64 at 512x512 and 512x480; 48 = 48 at 500x332 (8 x 6).
  * Leaves `md_encode_block` = `leaf_funnel::evaluate_leaf`: 13217 / 7995 /
    7285 / 1681 / 984 / ... exact everywhere identical. (The 2026-09-04
    record's `md_stage_0` is NOT a per-leaf count on screen content — C calls
    it once per candidate CLASS, 2627 for 1681 leaves at screen_terminal p6 —
    the join now uses `md_encode_block`.)
  * MDS0 SATD `hadamard_path` = `predict::hadamard_satd`: 474,718 = 474,718
    (photo_cid p2) and exact on every identical cell; the 4x4 / 8x8 / 32x32
    hadamard kernels exact. The 16x16 row reads 1.13-3.5x ONLY because the
    port's `aom_hadamard_32x32` calls `aom_hadamard_16x16` four times where
    C's 32x32 AVX2 does not go through the exported 16x16 symbol:
    71,672 - 4 x 2,046 = 63,488 = C's 63,488 (photo_cid p2), and the same
    identity holds on every cell. Not a finding; noted in the join.
  * PD0 recursion `pick_partition_pd0` = `Pd0Ctx::pick_q` (both recursion
    levels summed) and PD0 quantize `_light` = `pd0::tx_quant_core`: exact.
  * FINAL COMMITS: MDS1 luma `av1_quantize_b_facade_ii` =
    `quantize_b_raster` (281,598 = 281,598 at photo_cid p2; 5,834 = 5,834 at
    p6); MDS3 candidates `perform_tx_partitioning` = `mds3::eval_candidate`
    (91,350 = 91,350 p2; 2,316 = 2,316 p6); `full_loop_core` = eval_candidate
    + quantize_b_raster (372,948 = 372,948) — this is the join the mds1skip
    record established (C's full_loop_core is MDS1 AND MDS3), and it holds
