=================== THE THREE QUESTIONS, ANSWERED ===================

1. `txt_search -> tx_unit` promotion rule (fix 0ba430ee) — HOLDS on real
   content. C admits a LARGER fraction of its tx-type trials on photos than on
   the gradient (tx_type_search -> quantize_inv_quantize / tx_type_search ->
   estimate_transform: 2,753,262 / 3,445,449 = 79.9 % photo_cid, 73.8 %
   photo_clic, 77.7 % photo_clic500, vs 55.4 % gradient), so the screen is
   doing LESS filtering here, and the port tracks it: total forward
   transforms port/C 0.998 (cid) / 1.015 (clic) / 1.016 (clic500), total
   quantizer calls 0.993 / 1.013 / 1.014, RDOQ 0.998 / 1.009 / 1.005. The
   port's screen is an inlined loop with no symbol, so its promoted count is
   not directly countable; a mis-promotion would have to be cancelled to
   within 1.5 % by an equal and opposite error elsewhere in the same totals,
   which is not a mechanism. At p6: 1.008 / 1.052 / 1.051 (transforms). The
   1-5 % the port sits ABOVE C on the glitter image is real and unattributed
   (C's `estimate_transform` is 4,222,105 there, the port's
   `fwd_txfm2d_dispatch` 4,286,185: +64,080 calls); it is not the old 1.8x.

2. `run_mds1` at p10 — ZERO on all six contents (both0 in the TSV), and
   `full_loop_core` = `eval_candidate` at p10 on all six (886 / 787 / 793 /
   558 / 1294 / 972). The skip condition is NOT content-dependent; C's
   `enable_skipping_mds1` at nic level 11 fires on every leaf of a photo and
   a screenshot exactly as it does on the gradient. `tx_unit_inner` =
   `svt_aom_quantize_inv_quantize` at p10 on the photos (3752 = 3752,
   3648 = 3648, 2521 = 2521); on the two screen cells at p10 the port is
   BELOW C (4240 / 4395 and 3037 / 3910 — C's encode pass re-quantizes
   there; a C-side extra, not a port one).

3. `eval_candidate` vs `full_loop_core` — exact at every preset on every
   identical cell (see controls). The "2.307x MDS3 candidates at p10" row in
   the TSV for gradient (886 / 384) and lineart (972 / 473) is the SAME
   misjoin the mds1skip record closed: `perform_dct_dct_tx` has no symbol at
   -O3 (inlined into `full_loop_core`), so the `perform_tx_partitioning`
   count alone under-counts C's MDS3 at p10. Read the `full_loop_core` row.

