No MD-search edge crosses 1.5x. "Repeated work" in the call-graph-shape
sense (the port calling a kernel more often than C for the same output) is
now confined to three places, and only one of them grew with content:

  A. RESIDUAL PER TX-TYPE TRIAL — GREW. `svt_aom_residual_kernel` (all C
     callers) vs `residual::residual_i32`:
       p2:  gradient 1.383 | cid 2.143 | clic 2.184 | clic500 2.012 | (term 1.371, graph 1.180: ident=N)
       p6:  gradient 0.948 | cid 1.394 | clic 1.289 | clic500 1.315 | term 0.941 | graph 0.934
       p10: 1.000 | 0.977 | 0.975 | 0.996 | 0.760 | 0.880
     C derives the residual ONCE per (tx-depth, TXB) — `perform_tx_partitioning`
     (product_coding_loop.c:5337, 496,519x at photo_cid p2) and `full_loop_core`
     (458,000x) — and every tx-type candidate transforms that buffer. The port
     derives it once per TRIAL inside `tx_unit_inner`
     (leaf_funnel/tx_pipeline.rs:508, 4,238,186x). The ratio is the mean
     number of tx-type trials per TXB, which is ~2.1 on textured photos and
     ~1.4 on the gradient; that is why it grew. Ir: `residual_i32` inclusive
     1,502,206,698 = 3.05 % of the port's photo_cid p2 total, of which the
     excess calls are (1 - 1/2.143) = 53 % -> ~1.6 % of the port's Ir at p2
     on a photo (~1.7 % on clic). At p6 ~0.3 %, at p10 nil. Already named
     as open in callcount_txtscreen's "WHAT IS NOT FIXED"; this measures it.
     Fix shape unchanged: hoist the residual out of `txt_search`'s per-type
     loop (an optional precomputed-residual argument to `tx_unit`).

  B. THE ALLOCATOR — GREW 7x. `malloc+calloc+free` port/C:
       p2:  gradient 1,339x (3,483,642) | cid 9,292x (24,169,160) | clic 8,473x | clic500 6,325x
       p6:  125x | 216x | 185x | 143x | term 27x | graph 21x
       p10:  40x |  38x |  38x |  26x | term 52x | graph 41x
     C is 2,524-2,601 calls at EVERY cell (410 malloc / 781 calloc / 1,410
     free at 512x512: one-time setup, preset- and content-independent). The
     port's traffic scales with trials. Inclusive Ir on photo_cid p2:
     `__rust_alloc_zeroed` 992,259,808 (2.02 %) + `__rust_dealloc` 634,082,945
