  C. CDEF DIRECTION SEARCH — 2x BY COUNT, CONTENT-INDEPENDENT, TINY.
     `cdef::cdef_find_dir` 8,192 = 4,096 from `cdef::filter_fb_packed` (the
     search) + 4,096 from `cdef::apply_cdef_frame` (the apply); C's
     `svt_aom_cdef_find_dir_dual_avx2` 2,048 calls x 2 blocks = 4,096, all
     from `svt_cdef_filter_fb` — C computes each 8x8's direction once and
     caches it (`dirinit`, cdef.c:340/367); the port recomputes it in the
     apply (cdef.rs:460/666 vs :1081/1176). 17,539,072 Ir (0.04 % at p2,
     ~0.7 % at p6) — and per block the port's find_dir is ~10x C's
     (2,140 vs 208 Ir). Same on every content including gradient (3.98x).

Edges that are 1:1 BY COUNT but where the port's Ir per call is far above
C's — kernel findings, surfaced by real content, and NOT repeated work:

