  D. WIENER `compute_stats` — 127x PER CALL, CONTENT-INDEPENDENT, HALF OF p6.
     Both sides call it 6 times per 512x512 frame (4 at 500x332). Port
     `svtav1_dsp::restoration::compute_stats` (its `__arcane_..._impl_v3`
     AVX2 arm) is 746,546,988 Ir on EVERY 512x512 cell — gradient, both
     photos, the screenshot — at p2 and at p6 (472,802,392 at 500x332); C's
     `svt_av1_compute_stats_avx2` -> `compute_stats_win5_avx2`
     (pickrst_avx2.c:775) is 5,873,732 for the same six calls (photo_cid
     p6). Port `restoration::search_restoration_still_bd` inclusive:
     790.6 M = 33.0 % of photo_cid p6, 47.1 % of screen_terminal p6,
     55.2 % of lineart_graph p6, 49.2 % of gradient p6; C's whole
     `restoration_seg_search` is 8.15 M (1.16 %). With it removed the p6
     port/C ratio is 2.27x (cid) / 2.50x (term) instead of 3.40x / 4.72x —
     i.e. the p6 ratio being the worst of the three presets on every
     content is mostly this one stage. At p2 it is 2.1 % (photo) / 8.5 %
     (gradient) of the port's Ir; at p10 LR is off. `perf_still_attrib_
     2026-09-03` reported this kernel at 5.1x on aarch64 NEON and a row-pair
     fix landed there; on x86 the `_v3` arm is 127x per call against C's
     AVX2. NOT resolved here (no fix in a measure-only chunk); it is the
     next kernel to open on x86, ahead of anything in this record's count
     findings by a factor of ten at p6.

