and the zero-residual distortion as two calls; the port's `sse` covers both);
`svt_aom_full_loop_uv` 360,189 vs `chroma::eval_uv` 128,900 on photo_cid p2
(C's CFL alpha search goes through full_loop_uv 211,831 times; the port's
alpha loop does not call eval_uv); `txb_estimate_coeff_bits` vs `ccost_log`
0.65-0.90 (C's entry counts eob==0 shortcuts); inverse transforms at p10
0.51-0.63 (C's encode pass); `get_eob_cost` 0.80-0.87 at p2 on photos.

=================== CORRECTIONS TO THE PRIOR RECORDS ===================

1. callcount_2026-09-04's "inverse-transform dispatcher inflated 2.031x
   (p2) / 1.658x / 1.613x, does NOT converge at p10, a SEPARATE
   not-yet-attributed source" was a MISJOIN. It compared the port's total
   against `svt_av1_lowbd_inv_txfm2d_add_ssse3`, which is a SUB-dispatch
   (C's `svt_av1_inv_txfm_add_avx2` sends some sizes to AVX2 kernels that
   never enter the ssse3 entry). Against C's per-block wrapper
   `svt_aom_inv_transform_recon8bit` the port is 0.973 (p2), 0.844 (p6),
   0.543 (p10) on the gradient and 0.96-0.98 / 0.87-0.91 / 0.51-0.63 on
   real content — at or BELOW C at every cell. There is no inverse-
   transform call-count excess. (The old ssse3 row is kept in the TSV,
   labelled, so the two can be compared: it reads 0.99 on the photos.)
2. `md_stage_0` is per candidate class, not per leaf (above). The leaf
   control is `md_encode_block`.
3. `perform_dct_dct_tx` has no symbol in the -O3 oracle; the mds1skip
   record's "502 perform_dct_dct_tx" was an edge-derived number. At p10 the
   MDS3 join is `full_loop_core` alone.
4. Gradient re-baseline at 600c5177 (rustc 1.98.1) vs the records at
   708ef6386+fix / a1a32ca2f+fix (rustc 1.97.1): p2 11,767,652,265 vs
   11,788,718,910 (-0.18 %), p6 1,605,735,574 vs 1,607,135,446 (-0.09 %),
   p10 158,270,546 vs 159,339,453 (-0.67 %); C 4,424,517,108 /
   313,617,813 / 62,749,980 vs 4,424,517,561 / 313,618,266 / 62,749,694
   (same binary; <0.001 %). Every count in the txtscreen and mds1skip TSVs
   reproduces here to the unit where re-checked (SB 64, MDS1 commit 67,249,
   eval_candidate 9,165, optimize_b 260,098 / 7,857 / 1,110, quantizer
   373,254 / 15,600 / 2,882, allocator 3,483,642 vs 3,483,661). The
   toolchain bump is inert at this precision.

=================== PORT/C Ir TOTALS PER CELL (for the perf-status picture) ===================

            p2                          p6                       p10
  gradient  2.660 (11.77 G / 4.42 G)    5.120 (1.61 G / 0.31 G)  2.522 (158 M / 63 M)
  photo_cid 1.805 (49.17 G / 27.25 G)   3.395 (2.40 G / 0.71 G)  1.803 (185 M / 103 M)
  photo_clic 1.835 (48.74 G / 26.56 G)  3.440 (2.38 G / 0.69 G)  1.799 (180 M / 100 M)
  clic500   1.824 (32.24 G / 17.67 G)   3.343 (1.56 G / 0.47 G)  1.816 (122 M / 67 M)
  terminal  2.206* (14.01 G / 6.35 G)   4.723 (1.68 G / 0.36 G)  2.192 (138 M / 63 M)
  graph     2.444* (7.22 G / 2.96 G)    5.794 (1.34 G / 0.23 G)  2.477 (133 M / 54 M)
  (* ident=N)
The gradient OVERSTATES the p2 and p10 gaps (2.66x / 2.52x vs 1.80x / 1.80x
on photos): on the gradient most of the port's fixed overhead (LR stats,
allocator setup, helpers) sits over very little C work. It UNDERSTATES
nothing at p2. At p6 every content is 3.3-5.8x and the fixed 790 M Ir of
Wiener stats is 33-55 % of it.

=================== WHAT IS AND IS NOT ESTABLISHED ===================

ESTABLISHED: everything in the tables above, on 16 byte-identical cells, with
controls that passed. The three fixed mechanisms hold on textured photos, a
screenshot and line art. The residual and allocator counts grow with texture;
the compute_stats cost does not depend on content at all.
NOT ESTABLISHED: any wall-clock figure (no paired A/B run here — Ir on
r7900x is the record); the mechanism of the +1.5 % forward-transform excess
on the glitter image; why the port's `compute_stats` v3 arm costs 124 M Ir
per call (kernel not read in this chunk); anything about the two divergent
screen cells beyond that they diverge; 10-bit; video/inter; any qp but 40;
any preset but 2/6/10. The screen_terminal / lineart_graph p2 counts are
recorded but are NOT ratios (different work).
